Chapter: TavernBoard
  cites Uoaix chapter GameSkillsItems
  cites Uoaix chapter GameVendorState
  cites Uoaix chapter TavernBackgammon
  cites Games chapter Backgammon

 The Blue Boar's backgammon board (UOAIX-178, Damian 2026-10-09): TILEDATA "backgammon board" 0x0E1C mid-way along the
 tavern's long table (STATICS0.MUL table 0x0B76..0x0B75 at x 1497, y 1685 to 1689, z 20, height 6; benches at x 1496 and
 1498), a container the 1.25 client draws with gump 0x92E (282x210). Its checkers are white 0x3584 and black 0x358B
 (ARTIDX), set out once in Backgammon.codex's opening position and then moved freely, as ServUO's boards are.
  tbd-art : Integer = #0E1C
  tbd-gump : Integer = #092E
  tbd-white : Integer = #3584
  tbd-black : Integer = #358B
 Gump 0x92E's field spans x 43..240 in twelve points a half about 16.4 px wide (column c centred near 51 + c * 16.4),
 the top points y 5..80 and the bottom y 130..203. Backgammon.codex's index 0 is White's 1-point, bottom right; 11 is
 bottom left, 12 top left, 23 top right. A stack grows from the point's rim toward the bar, 12 px a checker.
  tbd-x-at : Integer -> Integer
  tbd-x-at (point) = let c = if point < 12 then 11 - point else point - 12 in 51 + c * 164 / 10 - 7
  tbd-y-at : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-y-at (point) (k) = if point < 12 then 188 - k * 12 else 8 + k * 12
  tbd-find : WorldTable, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-find (world) (serial) = if serial == 0 then 0
    else if (when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> False is Ok (o) -> o.kind == 2 & o.graphic == tbd-art & o.container == 0) then serial
    else tbd-find world (world-tile-next world serial)
  tbd-piece : GsiState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-piece (items) (board) (art) (x) (y) =
    when world-create items.world (WorldObject { serial = 0, kind = 2, x = x, y = y, z = 0, graphic = art, hue = 0, container = board, amount = 1, health = 0 })
      is Err (_) -> 0
      is Ok (serial) -> if gsi-register items serial 0 0 True False /= 0 then 0 else 1
  tbd-stack : GsiState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-stack (items) (board) (art) (point) (n) (k) = if k >= n then 0
    else tbd-piece items board art (tbd-x-at point) (tbd-y-at point k) + tbd-stack items board art point n (k + 1)
  tbd-points : GsiState, Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-points (items) (board) (points) (i) = if i >= list-length points then 0
    else let v = list-at points i
    in let n = if v < 0 then 0 - v else v
    in tbd-stack items board (if v > 0 then tbd-white else tbd-black) i n 0 + tbd-points items board points (i + 1)
 A checker dropped inside the field lands on the nearest point, on top of that point's stack (at most the sixth slot,
 where a taller stack overlaps); a drop on a side tray or the bar keeps the client's position.
  tbd-point-at : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-point-at (x) (y) = if x + 7 < 43 | x + 7 > 240 | (y + 7 > 88 & y + 7 < 122) then -1
    else let c = min 11 (max 0 ((x + 7 - 43) * 10 / 164))
    in if y + 7 <= 88 then 12 + c else 11 - c
  tbd-stacked : WorldTable, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-stacked (world) (serial) (x) (moving) = if serial == 0 then 0
    else let here = when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (o) -> if o.serial /= moving & tbd-checker o.graphic & tbd-zone o.x o.y == x then 1 else 0
    in here + tbd-stacked world (world-next-sibling world serial) x moving
  tbd-checker : Integer -> Boolean
  tbd-checker (art) = art == tbd-white | art == tbd-black
  tbd-put16 : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  tbd-put16 (p) (at) (v) = list-set-at (list-set-at p at (bit-and (bit-shr v 8) 255)) (at + 1) (bit-and v 255)
  tbd-snap : GsiState, List Integer -> List Integer
  tbd-snap (items) (packet) = if list-length packet /= 14 | list-at packet 0 /= 8 then packet
    else let target = gp-u32 packet 10
    in let moving = gp-u32 packet 1
    in let board = when world-get items.world target is Err (_) -> False is Ok (b) -> b.kind == 2 & b.graphic == tbd-art
    in let checker = when world-get items.world moving is Err (_) -> False is Ok (c) -> tbd-checker c.graphic
    in let point = if board & checker then tbd-point-at (gp-u16 packet 5) (gp-u16 packet 7) else -1
    in if point < 0 then packet
    else let x = tbd-x-at point
    in let k = min 5 (tbd-stacked items.world (world-first-child items.world target) point moving)
    in tbd-put16 (tbd-put16 packet 5 x) 7 (tbd-y-at point k)
 TILEDATA "dice and cup" 0x0FA7 stands at each end of the board, White's to the north and Black's to the south, and the
 server rolls them.
  tbd-dice-art : Integer = #0FA7
 Every backgammon set in the world is a live table (UOAIX-178, Damian 2026-10-09: "fix up all the other backgammon sets
 in the game too"): a board at x, y, z with a dice cup each side of it along dx, dy (White's at minus, Black's at plus).
 The first is the Blue Boar's long table (STATICS0.MUL table x 1497, y 1685 to 1689, top z 26). The rest stand where
 the decoration (britannia.dwd, ServUO Decoration) set a backgammon board 0x0E1C or folded game 0x0FAD, at the z of the
 dice cup 0x0FA7 beside it, toward that cup; a set with no cup beside it takes dy 1. premises.cfg clears each scenery set.
  TbdSet = record { x : Integer, y : Integer, z : Integer, dx : Integer, dy : Integer }
  tbd-set : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> TbdSet
  tbd-set (x) (y) (z) (dx) (dy) = TbdSet { x = x, y = y, z = z, dx = dx, dy = dy }
  tbd-sets : List TbdSet = [tbd-set 1497 1687 26 0 1, tbd-set 558 2188 4 0 -1, tbd-set 1402 1686 34 0 1, tbd-set 1440 3769 4 0 1,
    tbd-set 1452 3779 4 0 1, tbd-set 1497 1678 24 0 1, tbd-set 1534 1431 59 -1 0, tbd-set 1540 1749 39 1 0, tbd-set 1550 1762 16 0 1,
    tbd-set 1554 1763 14 0 1, tbd-set 1626 1587 4 0 -1, tbd-set 1807 2805 4 -1 0, tbd-set 1814 2806 24 0 -1, tbd-set 1933 2788 4 0 -1,
    tbd-set 1985 2911 4 0 1, tbd-set 2043 2777 4 -1 0, tbd-set 2467 400 19 1 0, tbd-set 2486 398 19 0 -1, tbd-set 2674 2238 6 0 1,
    tbd-set 2903 916 4 0 -1, tbd-set 3035 3346 37 0 1, tbd-set 3762 1223 4 0 1]
  tbd-home : TbdSet = list-at tbd-sets 0
  tbd-cup-x : TbdSet, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-cup-x (s) (side) = if side == 0 then s.x - s.dx else s.x + s.dx
  tbd-cup-y : TbdSet, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-cup-y (s) (side) = if side == 0 then s.y - s.dy else s.y + s.dy
  tbd-cup-of : WorldTable, TbdSet, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-cup-of (world) (s) (side) = tbd-cup world (world-tile-first world (tbd-cup-x s side) (tbd-cup-y s side))
  tbd-board : WorldTable, TbdSet -> Integer
  tbd-board (world) (s) = tbd-find world (world-tile-first world s.x s.y)
 The set whose cup (side 0 or 1, as cup * 2 + side) or whose board a serial is, or -1.
  tbd-cup-set : WorldTable, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-cup-set (world) (serial) (i) = tbd-cup-in tbd-sets world serial i
 A list constant is built again at every mention (about 1 KB for tbd-sets), so each walk names it once.
  tbd-cup-in : List TbdSet, WorldTable, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-cup-in (sets) (world) (serial) (i) = if i >= list-length sets then -1
    else let s = list-at sets i
    in if tbd-cup-of world s 0 == serial then i * 2 else if tbd-cup-of world s 1 == serial then i * 2 + 1 else tbd-cup-in sets world serial (i + 1)
  tbd-board-set : WorldTable, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-board-set (world) (board) (i) = tbd-board-in tbd-sets world board i
  tbd-board-in : List TbdSet, WorldTable, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-board-in (sets) (world) (board) (i) = if i >= list-length sets | board == 0 then -1
    else if tbd-board world (list-at sets i) == board then i else tbd-board-in sets world board (i + 1)
  tbd-cup : WorldTable, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-cup (world) (serial) = if serial == 0 then 0
    else if (when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> False is Ok (o) -> o.kind == 2 & o.graphic == tbd-dice-art & o.container == 0) then serial
    else tbd-cup world (world-tile-next world serial)
  tbd-install-cup : GsiState, TbdSet, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-install-cup (items) (s) (side) = if tbd-cup-of items.world s side /= 0 | world-room items.world <= 0 then 0
    else when world-create items.world (WorldObject { serial = 0, kind = 2, x = tbd-cup-x s side, y = tbd-cup-y s side, z = s.z, graphic = tbd-dice-art, hue = 0, container = 0, amount = 1, health = 0 })
      is Err (_) -> 0
      is Ok (cup) -> if gsi-register items cup 0 0 False False /= 0 then 0 else let touched = world-touch items.world in 1
  tbd-die : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-die (now) (salt) = 1 + int-mod (bit-and (mix-bits now salt) #7FFFFFFF) 6
 Two players (UOAIX-178, Damian 2026-10-09: "the first two players to roll are the players, first rolls are for going
 first, everyone else spectates after the second roller roll to go first. then the game is locked until a winner or
 nobody plays a move for 5 minutes"). The first player to roll a cup takes that cup's side and rolls one die; the
 second, at the other cup, rolls one, the higher goes first (a tie is rolled again by the server) and the table locks.
 A seated player rolls two dice to start a turn: the first mover at once, the other once the mover's dice are spent or
 cannot be played. The table frees after a winner, or tbd-idle-ticks with no roll or move (the next roll finds it free).
 The seats and the tick of the last roll or move live in the owner's tavern buffer (an item's fields stop at 65535), three
 qwords a set in tbd-sets order: White's serial, Black's serial (0 an empty seat), the tick. White's cup's health holds,
 above its dice digits (base 7, under tbd-flag-unit), the phase (0 free, 1 opening rolls, 2 White to roll, 3 Black to roll,
 4 White moving, 5 Black moving). A restart frees every table.
  tbd-index : TbdSet, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-index (s) (i) = tbd-index-in tbd-sets s i
  tbd-index-in : List TbdSet, TbdSet, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-index-in (sets) (s) (i) = if i >= list-length sets then 0 else if (list-at sets i).x == s.x & (list-at sets i).y == s.y then i else tbd-index-in sets s (i + 1)
  tbd-tavern-bytes : Integer = 24 * 22
  tbd-idle-ticks : Integer = 300000
  tbd-health : WorldTable, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-health (world) (serial) = when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (o) -> o.health
  tbd-set-health : WorldTable, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-set-health (world) (serial) (h) = when world-get world serial
    is Err (_) -> 0
    is Ok (o) -> when world-update world (__record-set o "health" h) is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (_) -> 1
  tbd-seat : Integer, TbdSet, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-seat (t) (s) (side) = peek-qword t (tbd-index s 0 * 24 + side * 8)
  tbd-sit : Integer, TbdSet, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-sit (t) (s) (side) (serial) = poke-qword t (tbd-index s 0 * 24 + side * 8) serial
  tbd-phase : WorldTable, TbdSet -> Integer
  tbd-phase (world) (s) = int-mod (tbd-health world (tbd-cup-of world s 0) / tbd-flag-unit) 8
  tbd-last : Integer, TbdSet -> Integer
  tbd-last (t) (s) = peek-qword t (tbd-index s 0 * 24 + 16)
  tbd-stamp : Integer, TbdSet, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-stamp (t) (s) (now) = poke-qword t (tbd-index s 0 * 24 + 16) now
  tbd-set-phase : WorldTable, Integer, TbdSet, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-set-phase (world) (t) (s) (phase) (now) = let cup = tbd-cup-of world s 0
    in let stamped = tbd-stamp t s now
    in tbd-set-health world cup (int-mod (tbd-health world cup) tbd-flag-unit + tbd-flag-unit * phase)
  tbd-dice-of : WorldTable, TbdSet, Integer -> List Integer
  tbd-dice-of (world) (s) (side) = tbd-decode (int-mod (tbd-health world (tbd-cup-of world s side)) tbd-flag-unit) []
  tbd-mover : Integer -> Integer
  tbd-mover (phase) = if phase == 4 then 0 else if phase == 5 then 1 else -1
  tbd-stuck : WorldTable, TbdSet, Integer -> Boolean
  tbd-stuck (world) (s) (side) = let dice = tbd-dice-of world s side
    in let board = tbd-board world s
    in list-length dice == 0 | board == 0 | bg-ai-pick (tbd-position world board side) dice < 0
  tbd-colour : Integer -> Text
  tbd-colour (side) = if side == 0 then "White" else "Black"
  tbd-tell : Integer, Text -> Maybe GameReply
  tbd-tell (cup) (text) = Just (gs-reply [sip-message cup tbd-dice-art 6 text] "tavern:refused")
  tbd-say : Integer, Text -> Maybe GameReply
  tbd-say (cup) (text) = Just (gs-reply [sip-message cup tbd-dice-art 6 text] "tavern:dice")
 Clears both seats and both cups, and lays a fresh board.
  tbd-reset : GsiState, Integer, TbdSet -> Integer
  tbd-reset (items) (t) (s) = let world = items.world
    in let board = tbd-board world s
    in let cleared = if board == 0 then 0 else tbd-clear world (world-first-child world board)
    in let start = backgammon-new
    in let laid = if board == 0 then 0 else tbd-points items board start.points 0
    in let a = tbd-sit t s 0 0 + tbd-sit t s 1 0 + tbd-stamp t s 0
    in let b = tbd-set-health world (tbd-cup-of world s 0) 0
    in let c = tbd-set-health world (tbd-cup-of world s 1) 0
    in let touched = world-touch world in laid
  tbd-dice : GvWorld, GsiState, Integer, GameShard, GameInput, List Integer, Integer -> Maybe GameReply
  tbd-dice (v) (items) (t) (game) (input) (packet) (now) = if list-length packet /= 5 | list-at packet 0 /= 6 | input.mode /= 2 | input.session.phase /= 2 then None
    else let serial = bit-and (gp-u32 packet 1) #7FFFFFFF
    in let world = items.world
    in if serial /= 0 & tbd-side-checker world serial tbd-white then tbd-bear v items t game input serial True now
    else if serial /= 0 & tbd-side-checker world serial tbd-black then tbd-bear v items t game input serial False now
    else let found = if serial == 0 then -1 else tbd-cup-set world serial 0
    in if found < 0 then None
    else let s = list-at tbd-sets (found / 2)
    in let side = int-mod found 2
    in when world-get game.world input.session.serial
      is Err (_) -> None
      is Ok (m) -> if walk-abs (m.x - tbd-cup-x s side) > 2 | walk-abs (m.y - tbd-cup-y s side) > 2 then Just (gsi-denied "That is too far away.")
        else let idle = tbd-phase world s > 0 & now - tbd-last t s >= tbd-idle-ticks
        in let freed = if idle then tbd-reset items t s else 0
        in tbd-roll world t s serial side m.serial now idle
  tbd-roll : WorldTable, Integer, TbdSet, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean -> Maybe GameReply
  tbd-roll (world) (t) (s) (cup) (side) (player) (now) (idle) = let phase = tbd-phase world s
    in let mine = tbd-seat t s side
    in let theirs = tbd-seat t s (1 - side)
    in let one = tbd-die now (cup + player)
    in let two = tbd-die (now + 1) (cup + player * 3)
    in let lead = if idle then "The table stood idle five minutes and is free again. " else ""
    in if phase == 0 then
      (let sat = tbd-sit t s side player
      in let kept = tbd-keep world cup [one]
      in let opened = tbd-set-phase world t s 1 now
      in tbd-say cup (lead & tbd-colour side & " rolls " & show one & " to go first. The other cup's first roller plays " & tbd-colour (1 - side) & "."))
    else if phase == 1 then
      (if mine == player then tbd-tell cup "Wait for your opponent to roll the other cup."
      else if theirs == player then tbd-tell cup "You have rolled; wait for your opponent."
      else if mine /= 0 then tbd-tell cup "That side is taken; roll the other cup."
      else let sat = tbd-sit t s side player
      in let rolled = tbd-dice-of world s (1 - side)
      in let other = if list-length rolled == 0 then 0 else list-at rolled 0
      in let die = tbd-unequal one other now 0
      in let first = if die > other then side else 1 - side
      in let a = tbd-keep world (tbd-cup-of world s 0) []
      in let b = tbd-keep world (tbd-cup-of world s 1) []
      in let locked = tbd-set-phase world t s (if first == 0 then 2 else 3) now
      in tbd-say cup (tbd-colour side & " rolls " & show die & (if die /= one then " after a tie" else "") & " against " & show other & ". "
        & tbd-colour first & " goes first. The table is locked; everyone else watches."))
    else if player /= tbd-seat t s 0 & player /= tbd-seat t s 1 then tbd-tell cup "This game is in play; you are watching."
    else if mine /= player then tbd-tell cup "Roll your own cup."
    else if tbd-mover phase == side then tbd-tell cup (if tbd-stuck world s side then "Your opponent rolls next." else "Play your roll first.")
    else let opens = (phase == 2 & side == 0) | (phase == 3 & side == 1)
    in let passes = tbd-mover phase == 1 - side & tbd-stuck world s (1 - side)
    in if not (opens | passes) then tbd-tell cup (if tbd-mover phase >= 0 then "Your opponent has not played the roll." else "It is the other side's turn.")
    else let dice = if one == two then [one, one, one, one] else [one, two]
    in let cleared = tbd-keep world (tbd-cup-of world s (1 - side)) []
    in let kept = tbd-keep world cup dice
    in let moving = tbd-set-phase world t s (if side == 0 then 4 else 5) now
    in tbd-say cup (tbd-colour side & " rolls " & show one & " and " & show two & ".")
 An opening die equal to the other side's is rolled again (at most 16 times; then the next value up).
  tbd-unequal : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-unequal (die) (other) (now) (n) = if die /= other then die else if n >= 16 then int-mod other 6 + 1
    else tbd-unequal (tbd-die (now + 2 + n) (n * 7 + other)) other now (n + 1)
 The client keeps a drop inside gump 0x92E's container bounds, so a checker dropped toward a side tray lands on an edge
 point and is refused; a double-click on a checker of the mover's side bears it off with the smallest die the rules allow.
  tbd-side-checker : WorldTable, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  tbd-side-checker (world) (serial) (art) = when world-get world serial
    is Err (_) -> False
    is Ok (c) -> c.kind == 2 & c.graphic == art & (when world-get world c.container is Err (_) -> False is Ok (b) -> b.kind == 2 & b.graphic == tbd-art)
 Why a seated player may not move side's checkers now, or "" when it may.
  tbd-refusal : WorldTable, Integer, TbdSet, Integer, Integer -> Text
  tbd-refusal (world) (t) (s) (side) (serial) = let phase = tbd-phase world s
    in if phase < 2 then "Roll the dice first."
    else if serial /= tbd-seat t s 0 & serial /= tbd-seat t s 1 then "This game is in play; you are watching."
    else if tbd-seat t s side /= serial then "Those are your opponent's checkers."
    else if tbd-mover phase /= side | list-length (tbd-dice-of world s side) == 0 then "Roll the dice first."
    else ""
  tbd-bear : GvWorld, GsiState, Integer, GameShard, GameInput, Integer, Boolean, Integer -> Maybe GameReply
  tbd-bear (v) (items) (t) (game) (input) (serial) (white) (now) = when world-get items.world serial
    is Err (_) -> None
    is Ok (c) -> when world-get game.world input.session.serial
      is Err (_) -> None
      is Ok (m) -> let world = items.world
        in let found = tbd-board-set world c.container 0
        in if found < 0 then None
        else let s = list-at tbd-sets found
        in if walk-abs (m.x - s.x) > 2 | walk-abs (m.y - s.y) > 2 then Just (gsi-denied "That is too far away.")
        else let side = if white then 0 else 1
        in let refusal = tbd-refusal world t s side m.serial
        in let from = tbd-zone c.x c.y
        in if from == (0 - 3) then None
        else if refusal /= "" then Just (gs-reply [sip-message #FFFFFFFF #FFFF 6 refusal] "tavern:refused")
        else let dice = tbd-dice-of world s side
        in let die = if from < 0 then 0 else tbd-off-die (tbd-position world c.container side) dice from white 1
        in if die < 1 then Just (gs-reply [sip-message #FFFFFFFF #FFFF 6 "That checker cannot bear off with your roll."] "tavern:refused")
        else let spent = tbd-keep world (tbd-cup-of world s side) (tbd-without dice die 0 False [])
        in let stamped = tbd-stamp t s now
        in let moved = tbd-move-to world c.container serial (0 - 3) (if white then tbd-white else tbd-black)
        in Just (gs-reply (moved & tbd-settle v items t c.container) "tavern:off")
  tbd-move-to : WorldTable, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List (List Integer)
  tbd-move-to (world) (board) (serial) (zone) (art) = when world-get world serial
    is Err (_) -> []
    is Ok (c) -> let first = world-first-child world board
      in let x = if zone >= 0 then tbd-x-at zone else if zone == (0 - 2) then (if art == tbd-white then 124 else 144) else (if art == tbd-white then 10 else 258)
      in let k = if zone >= 0 then min 5 (tbd-stacked world first zone serial) else tbd-in-zone world first zone art
      in let y = if zone >= 0 then tbd-y-at zone k else if zone == (0 - 2) then 98 + min 2 k * 4 else 10 + min 14 k * 12
      in when world-update world (__record-set (__record-set c "x" x) "y" y)
        is Err (_) -> []
        is Ok (_) -> when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> [] is Ok (placed) -> [sip-item placed]
  tbd-position : WorldTable, Integer, Integer -> BackgammonBoard
  tbd-position (world) (board) (player) = let first = world-first-child world board
    in BackgammonBoard { points = tbd-count world first (tbd-zeros 24 []),
      bar-white = tbd-in-zone world first (0 - 2) tbd-white, bar-black = tbd-in-zone world first (0 - 2) tbd-black,
      off-white = tbd-in-zone world first (0 - 3) tbd-white, off-black = tbd-in-zone world first (0 - 3) tbd-black,
      current-player = player, cube = 1, cube-owner = (-1), offered = 0, dropped = (-1) }
 The cup's health holds the dice still to play, one base-7 digit each (a double is four), so the board knows the roll.
  tbd-encode : List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-encode (dice) (i) = if i >= list-length dice then 0 else list-at dice i + 7 * tbd-encode dice (i + 1)
  tbd-decode : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  tbd-decode (code) (out) = if code <= 0 then out else tbd-decode (code / 7) (list-push out (int-mod code 7))
  tbd-keep : WorldTable, Integer, List Integer -> Integer
  tbd-keep (world) (cup) (dice) = when world-get world cup
    is Err (_) -> 0
    is Ok (o) -> when world-update world (__record-set o "health" (tbd-encode dice 0 + tbd-flag-unit * (o.health / tbd-flag-unit))) is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (_) -> 1
  tbd-flag-unit : Integer = 2401
  tbd-without : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, List Integer -> List Integer
  tbd-without (dice) (die) (i) (gone) (out) = if i >= list-length dice then out
    else if not gone & list-at dice i == die then tbd-without dice die (i + 1) True out
    else tbd-without dice die (i + 1) gone (list-push out (list-at dice i))
 Backgammon.codex's position is rebuilt from the checkers standing on points (positive White, negative Black); checkers
 on the bar or a tray are not counted, so moves onto or off them are not refereed.
  tbd-count : WorldTable, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  tbd-count (world) (serial) (points) = if serial == 0 then points
    else let next = world-next-sibling world serial
    in when world-get world serial
      is Err (_) -> tbd-count world next points
      is Ok (c) -> let p = if tbd-checker c.graphic then tbd-point-at c.x c.y else -1
        in if p < 0 then tbd-count world next points
        else tbd-count world next (list-set-at points p (list-at points p + (if c.graphic == tbd-white then 1 else -1)))
 A checker's zone on the gump: its point, -2 on the bar (the field's middle band), -3 on a side tray (borne off).
  tbd-zone : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-zone (x) (y) = if x + 7 < 43 | x + 7 > 240 then (0 - 3) else if y + 7 > 88 & y + 7 < 122 then (0 - 2) else tbd-point-at x y
  tbd-in-zone : WorldTable, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-in-zone (world) (serial) (zone) (art) = if serial == 0 then 0
    else let here = when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (c) -> if c.graphic == art & tbd-zone c.x c.y == zone then 1 else 0
    in here + tbd-in-zone world (world-next-sibling world serial) zone art
  tbd-off-die : BackgammonBoard, List Integer, Integer, Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-off-die (b) (dice) (from) (white) (d) = if d > 6 then 0
    else if bg-has-die dice d 0 & (if white then from - d < 0 else from + d >= 24) & bg-legal b dice from d then d
    else tbd-off-die b dice from white (d + 1)
 A refereed move onto a point holding one opposing checker hits it: the server moves that checker onto the bar, White's
 left of centre and Black's right, before the mover lands.
  tbd-at : WorldTable, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-at (world) (serial) (zone) (art) = if serial == 0 then 0
    else if (when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> False is Ok (c) -> c.graphic == art & tbd-zone c.x c.y == zone) then serial
    else tbd-at world (world-next-sibling world serial) zone art
  tbd-hit : GsiState, List Integer -> List (List Integer)
  tbd-hit (items) (packet) = if list-length packet /= 14 | list-at packet 0 /= 8 then []
    else let board = gp-u32 packet 10
    in let to = tbd-zone (gp-u16 packet 5) (gp-u16 packet 7)
    in when world-get items.world (gp-u32 packet 1)
      is Err (_) -> []
      is Ok (c) -> let from = tbd-zone c.x c.y
        in if to < 0 | c.container /= board | not (tbd-checker c.graphic) | (from < 0 & from /= (0 - 2)) | from == to then []
        else let other = if c.graphic == tbd-white then tbd-black else tbd-white
        in let first = world-first-child items.world board
        in if tbd-in-zone items.world first to other /= 1 then []
        else let hit = tbd-at items.world first to other
        in let k = tbd-in-zone items.world first (0 - 2) other
        in when world-get items.world hit
          is Err (_) -> []
          is Ok (h) -> let placed = __record-set (__record-set h "x" (if other == tbd-white then 124 else 144)) "y" (98 + min 2 k * 4)
            in when world-update items.world placed is Err (_) -> [] is Ok (_) -> [sip-item placed]
  tbd-zeros : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  tbd-zeros (n) (out) = if n == 0 then out else tbd-zeros (n - 1) (list-push out 0)
 A checker moved between two points on the board must use a die still in its side's cup: 0 lets an unrefereed drop
 through, minus the die lets a legal move through, 1 refuses an illegal move (the bar and a tray are not drop targets),
 2 refuses a move before that side's roll, 3 a checker moved by a watcher, 4 a checker of the side not on turn, 5 the
 opponent's checker.
  tbd-referee : GsiState, Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-referee (items) (t) (packet) (serial) = if list-length packet /= 14 | list-at packet 0 /= 8 then 0
    else let board = gp-u32 packet 10
    in let to = tbd-zone (gp-u16 packet 5) (gp-u16 packet 7)
    in when world-get items.world (gp-u32 packet 1)
      is Err (_) -> 0
      is Ok (c) -> let from = if c.container == board & tbd-checker c.graphic then tbd-zone c.x c.y else (0 - 9)
        in let isboard = when world-get items.world board is Err (_) -> False is Ok (b) -> b.graphic == tbd-art
        in let found = tbd-board-set items.world board 0
        in if not isboard | found < 0 | from == (0 - 9) | from == to then 0
        else let world = items.world
        in let s = list-at tbd-sets found
        in let white = c.graphic == tbd-white
        in let side = if white then 0 else 1
        in let phase = tbd-phase world s
        in if phase < 2 then 2
        else if serial /= tbd-seat t s 0 & serial /= tbd-seat t s 1 then 3
        else if tbd-seat t s side /= serial then 5
        else if tbd-mover phase /= side then 4
        else if from == (0 - 3) | to == (0 - 2) then 1
        else let dice = tbd-dice-of world s side
        in if list-length dice == 0 then 2
        else let first = world-first-child items.world board
        in let b = BackgammonBoard { points = tbd-count items.world first (tbd-zeros 24 []),
          bar-white = tbd-in-zone items.world first (0 - 2) tbd-white, bar-black = tbd-in-zone items.world first (0 - 2) tbd-black,
          off-white = tbd-in-zone items.world first (0 - 3) tbd-white, off-black = tbd-in-zone items.world first (0 - 3) tbd-black,
          current-player = side, cube = 1, cube-owner = (-1), offered = 0, dropped = (-1) }
        in let source = if from == (0 - 2) then bg-bar-from else from
        in let die = if to == (0 - 3) then (if from < 0 then 0 else tbd-off-die b dice from white 1)
          else if from == (0 - 2) then (if white then 24 - to else to + 1)
          else if white then from - to else to - from
        in if die < 1 | die > 6 | not (bg-legal b dice source die) then 1
        else 0 - die
 A refereed die is spent once the checker stands in the zone it was dropped on, so a drop the item layer refuses keeps
 it; the move restarts the table's idle clock.
  tbd-spend : GsiState, Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-spend (items) (t) (packet) (die) (now) = when world-get items.world (gp-u32 packet 1)
    is Err (_) -> 0
    is Ok (c) -> if c.container /= gp-u32 packet 10 | tbd-zone c.x c.y /= tbd-zone (gp-u16 packet 5) (gp-u16 packet 7) then 0
      else let found = tbd-board-set items.world c.container 0
      in if found < 0 then 0
      else let s = list-at tbd-sets found
      in let side = if c.graphic == tbd-white then 0 else 1
      in let dice = tbd-dice-of items.world s side
      in let stamped = tbd-stamp t s now
      in tbd-keep items.world (tbd-cup-of items.world s side) (tbd-without dice die 0 False [])
  tbd-install : GsiState -> Integer
  tbd-install (items) = tbd-install-from items 0
  tbd-install-from : GsiState, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-install-from (items) (i) = if i >= list-length tbd-sets then 0 else tbd-install-set items (list-at tbd-sets i) + tbd-install-from items (i + 1)
  tbd-install-set : GsiState, TbdSet -> Integer
  tbd-install-set (items) (s) = let cups = tbd-install-cup items s 0 + tbd-install-cup items s 1
    in if tbd-board items.world s /= 0 | world-room items.world < 31 then cups
    else when world-create items.world (WorldObject { serial = 0, kind = 2, x = s.x, y = s.y, z = s.z, graphic = tbd-art, hue = 0, container = 0, amount = 1, health = 0 })
      is Err (_) -> 0
      is Ok (board) -> if gsi-register items board 0 tbd-gump False False /= 0 then 0
        else let start = backgammon-new
        in let placed = tbd-points items board start.points 0
        in let touched = world-touch items.world in cups + 1 + placed
 Silas's house (the Sweet Dreams innkeeper, vendor 5 in bb-shops order) is paid for a round of drink.
  tbd-house : Integer = 5
  tbd-clear : WorldTable, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-clear (world) (serial) = if serial == 0 then 0
    else let next = world-next-sibling world serial
    in let gone = when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (c) -> if tbd-checker c.graphic then (when world-delete world serial is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (_) -> 1) else 0
    in gone + tbd-clear world next
 When either side has borne off all fifteen checkers the winner is named, and the table frees with a fresh board.
  tbd-settle : GvWorld, GsiState, Integer, Integer -> List (List Integer)
  tbd-settle (v) (items) (t) (board) = let found = tbd-board-set items.world board 0
    in if found < 0 then []
    else let s = list-at tbd-sets found
    in let first = world-first-child items.world board
    in let white = tbd-in-zone items.world first (0 - 3) tbd-white
    in let black = tbd-in-zone items.world first (0 - 3) tbd-black
    in if white < 15 & black < 15 then []
    else let points = bg-points (tbd-position items.world board 0)
    in let freed = tbd-reset items t s
    in [sip-message board tbd-art 6 ((if white >= 15 then "White" else "Black") & " wins " & show (max 1 points) & (if points > 1 then " points." else " point.")),
      sip-message board tbd-art 6 "The table is free; roll a cup to play."]
 A fresh game (every checker on its opening point) offers the stake first: the first roll is the offer, and only the
 roll after it, under turn flag 2, starts play.
  tbd-same : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  tbd-same (a) (b) (i) = if i >= list-length a then True else list-at a i == list-at b i & tbd-same a b (i + 1)
  tbd-fresh : WorldTable, Integer -> Boolean
  tbd-fresh (world) (board) = let p = tbd-position world board 0
    in let start = backgammon-new
    in p.bar-white == 0 & p.bar-black == 0 & p.off-white == 0 & p.off-black == 0 & tbd-same p.points start.points 0
 The patron is a gambler standing on the inn floor beside the board, a saved world mobile told apart by its hue, as the
 Royal Minter is. His persona (TavernBackgammon.codex TbPatron) sets his play: he takes the engine's best move with
 probability tb-strength / 1000 (skill less drink) and otherwise the first legal one (tb-first).
  tbd-patron-x : Integer = 1497
  tbd-patron-y : Integer = 1616
  tbd-patron-z : Integer = 20
  tbd-patron-hue : Integer = #0459
  tbd-persona : TbPatron = TbPatron { identity = 1, purse = 0, npc = True, skill = 700, drink = 0, appetite = 600, wager-limit = 100 }
  tbd-gambler : WorldTable, Integer -> Integer
  tbd-gambler (world) (serial) = if serial == 0 then 0
    else if (when world-get world serial is Err (_) -> False is Ok (o) -> o.kind == 1 & o.hue == tbd-patron-hue & o.container == 0) then serial
    else tbd-gambler world (world-tile-next world serial)
  tbd-name : GsiState, List Integer -> Maybe GameReply
  tbd-name (items) (packet) = if list-length packet /= 5 | list-at packet 0 /= 9 then None
    else let serial = bit-and (gp-u32 packet 1) #7FFFFFFF
    in if serial == 0 | tbd-gambler items.world (world-tile-first items.world tbd-patron-x tbd-patron-y) /= serial then None
    else let cup = tbd-cup items.world (world-tile-first items.world (tbd-cup-x tbd-home 0) (tbd-cup-y tbd-home 0))
    in let rounds = when world-get items.world cup is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (o) -> o.health / tbd-drink-unit
    in Just (gs-reply [sip-message serial 0 6 ("Silas the gambler" & (if rounds >= 3 then " (drunk)" else if rounds >= 1 then " (merry)" else ""))] "tavern:name")
 Above the turn flag the cup's health holds Silas's drink, one level (250) per round bought, at most four; settling a
 game clears it. Drink dulls his play (tb-strength) and warms him to a stake (tb-interest).
  tbd-drink-unit : Integer = 9604
  tbd-drunk : Integer -> TbPatron
  tbd-drunk (health) = TbPatron { identity = 1, purse = 0, npc = True, skill = 700, drink = 250 * min 4 (health / tbd-drink-unit),
    appetite = 600, wager-limit = 100 }
  tbd-round-price : Integer = 5
  tbd-round : GvWorld, GsiState, GameShard, GameInput, Integer -> Maybe GameReply
  tbd-round (v) (items) (game) (input) (gambler) = when world-get game.world input.session.serial
    is Err (_) -> None
    is Ok (m) -> if walk-abs (m.x - tbd-patron-x) > 2 | walk-abs (m.y - tbd-patron-y) > 2 then Just (gsi-denied "That is too far away.")
      else let cup = tbd-cup items.world (world-tile-first items.world (tbd-cup-x tbd-home 0) (tbd-cup-y tbd-home 0))
      in let at = gv-player v input.session.serial 0
      in if cup == 0 | at < 0 | tbd-house >= list-length v.vendors then None
      else let health = when world-get items.world cup is Err (_) -> 0 is Ok (o) -> o.health
      in if health / tbd-drink-unit >= 4 then Just (gs-reply [sip-message gambler 0 6 "Silas pushes the cup away. 'No more for me.'"] "tavern:round")
      else let w = v.currency.world
      in let paid = eu-pay v.currency True (ep-actor w (list-at v.players at).actor).purse (ep-actor w (list-at v.vendors tbd-house).actor).purse tbd-round-price 0 0
      in if paid /= 0 then Just (gsi-denied ("A round costs " & show tbd-round-price & " copper."))
      else when world-get items.world cup
        is Err (_) -> None
        is Ok (o) -> when world-update items.world (__record-set o "health" (o.health + tbd-drink-unit))
          is Err (_) -> None
          is Ok (_) -> Just (gs-reply [sip-message gambler 0 6 "Silas drains the ale. 'Your health!'"] "tavern:round")
